  note = {Insights: Proposes an agentic-AI-enabled digital thread architecture that uses CASCaDE knowledge graphs, RAG, and GraphRAG to deliver trusted, explainable lifecycle traceability across requirements, design, test, manufacturing, and operations. \textbar\textbar{} TL;DR: This presentation shows how agentic AI layered over CASCaDE-based knowledge graphs enables adaptive, context-aware reasoning across the systems engineering lifecycle, improving traceability and decision support. \textbar\textbar{} Contributions: - Articulates a clear distinction between AI agents and agentic AI, emphasizing autonomy, intentionality, adaptivity, and accountability. - Positions CASCaDE (OMG) as a tool-neutral integration standard enabling a single source of truth across MBSE, PLM, CAD, and test tools. - Demonstrates how RAG and GraphRAG mitigate LLM hallucinations for lifecycle queries (e.g., untested requirements). - Defines knowledge graphs as the backbone of the digital thread using RDF triples. - Presents an end-to-end reasoning stack (LLM + RAG + GraphRAG + agentic coordination) for explainable SE decisions. \textbar\textbar{} Challenges: - Requires high-quality, well-governed lifecycle data to realize benefits. - Integration with legacy tools and data silos remains nontrivial. - Governance and accountability must be engineered for agentic autonomy. - Scaling knowledge graph maintenance across large programs can be resource-intensive.
