@misc{Traveller_Agile_Engineering_Agentic_Co_Modelers_2025,
  title = {Agile Engineering Enabled by Agentic Co-Modelers},
  author = {Traveller, Hart and Brechtel, Zeke and Massey, Steve},
  year = 2025,
  month = sep,
  howpublished = {SysGit industry research presentation},
  note = {Insights: Demonstrates that agentic co-modelers---AI systems tightly integrated with formal SysML v2 grammars, validation metrics, and simulation feedback---can dramatically accelerate model-based systems engineering while preserving physical and semantic correctness. \textbar\textbar{} TL;DR: This presentation shows how agentic AI pipelines can translate large volumes of technical documentation into validated SysML v2 models by combining LLMs with parsers, graph representations, and continuous correctness metrics. \textbar\textbar{} Contributions: - Defines a clear distinction between inventive vs. translative AI behavior, arguing that engineering AI should prioritize faithful information isomorphism over creative synthesis (pp. 30--35). - Introduces syntactic and semantic quality (SSQ) and validity (SSV) metrics to continuously score SysML model correctness (pp. 11--16). - Demonstrates an end-to-end pipeline converting historical MSR documentation into executable SysML models with rejection-and-repair loops driven by validation and simulation feedback (pp. 9--18). - Uses intermediary graph representations to support retrieval, mutation, traceability, and serialization back into SysML v2 (pp. 20--23). - Shows empirical improvements in syntax quality and validity when LLMs are guided by context, parsers, and formal grammars rather than free-form prompting (pp. 15--16). \textbar\textbar{} Challenges: - Physical realizability and quantitative validation remain significantly harder than syntactic correctness (p. 28). - Scaling human-in-the-loop review and traceability for agent decisions is still an open problem. - Managing inventiveness versus hallucination requires explicit constraints and evaluation criteria. - Integration into diverse enterprise MBSE toolchains requires governance and standardization.
\par
performing systems engineering with sysmlv2 and git. everything is in one repository with ci/cd included for val/ver.
\par
SysGit. Focuses on agentic AI systems for SysML v2 model generation, validation, and iterative refinement using formal syntax/semantic metrics},
